        "type": "group"
      },
      {
        "children": [
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "id": "sny6x9juqfhwb7e",
                "text": "A Note about Significant Figures and Logarithms"
              }
            ],
            "id": "mub5rqxghlpusbv",
            "type": "h2"
          },
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "text": "Significant figure rules for logarithms, such as pH and pOH, are consistent with our usual rules but may appear different due to the nature of logarithms. To illustrate, let's consider a solution with [H"
              },
              {
                "sub": true,
                "text": "3"
              },
              {
                "text": "O"
              },
              {
                "sup": true,
                "text": "+"
              },
              {
                "text": "] equal to 1.0 × 10"
              },
              {
                "sup": true,
                "text": "−5"
              },
              {
                "text": " M. This value has two significant figures (1 and 0), so when we calculate pH, the result should also have two significant figures. The negative log of 1.0 × 10"
              },
              {
                "sup": true,
                "text": "−5"
              },
              {
                "text": " is 5, which is the negative of the exponent when the H"
              },
              {
                "sub": true,
                "text": "3"
              },
              {
                "text": "O"
              },
              {
                "sup": true,
                "text": "+"
              },
              {
                "text": " concentration is written in scientific notation. (Recall that logarithms are essentially exponents, and we are using base 10.) Because our answer should have two significant figures and the exponent does not play a role in this calculation, we write the pH value as 5.00. The value to the left of the decimal point (5) corresponds to the exponent and is not a significant figure; the numbers to the right (0 and 0) are the significant values."
              }
            ],
            "id": "rt2876jmcxkv6bi",
            "type": "p"
          },
          {
            "caption": [
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "em": true,
                    "text": "[H"
                  },
                  {
                    "em": true,
                    "sub": true,
                    "text": "3"
                  },
                  {
                    "em": true,
                    "text": "O"
                  },
                  {
                    "em": true,
                    "sup": true,
                    "text": "+"
                  },
                  {
                    "em": true,
                    "text": "] = 1.0 × 10"
                  },
                  {
                    "em": true,
                    "sup": true,
                    "text": "−5"
                  },
                  {
                    "em": true,
                    "text": " M and pH = 5.00; both have two significant figures."
                  }
                ],
                "type": "p"
              }
            ],
            "children": [
              {
                "id": "nx2je2juv3sqn8s",
                "text": " ",
                "type": "text"
              }
            ],
            "id": "a12ahkvrrtc449c",
            "src": "https://d2xvti2irp4c7t.cloudfront.net/media/52/52163868d982d60b39af97e37b852931/pH_sig_figs.png",
            "type": "img",
            "width": "350"
          },
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "text": " In the first example above, the [H"
              },
              {
                "sub": true,
                "text": "3"
              },
              {
                "text": "O"
              },
              {
                "sup": true,
                "text": "+"
              },
              {
                "text": "] is given as 1.2 × 10"
              },
              {
                "sup": true,
                "text": "−3"
              },
              {
                "text": " M and the pH is given as 2.92. For logarithms, the value before the decimal point represents the exponent and the value after the decimal represents the significant figures. In this example, both the [H"
              },
              {
                "sub": true,
                "text": "3"
              },
              {
                "text": "O"
              },
              {
                "sup": true,
                "text": "+"
              },
              {
                "text": "] and the pH have two significant figures. "
              }
            ],
            "id": "xly1i77lcjcus0k",
            "type": "p"
          },
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "text": " Likewise, in the second example, the given pH value of 7.3 has one significant figure, which is why the [H"
              },
              {
                "sub": true,
                "text": "3"
              },
              {
                "text": "O"
              },
              {
                "sup": true,
                "text": "+"
              },
              {
                "text": "] is given in one significant figure, 5 × 10"
              },
              {
                "sup": true,
                "text": "−8"
              },
              {
                "text": " M."
              }
            ],
            "id": "ilyd0d43yozwpvu",
            "type": "p"
          }
        ],
