      {
        "children": [
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "id": "x8oua3hwdtgpkuq",
                "text": "Calculating pOH"
              }
            ],
            "id": "q9g1jvcs3l5xt2t",
            "type": "h1"
          }
        ],
        "id": "2536299432",
        "selection": {
          "anchor": {
            "offset": 0,
            "path": [
              0,
              0
            ]
          },
          "focus": {
            "offset": 0,
            "path": [
              1,
              0
            ]
          }
        },
        "type": "content"
      },
      {
        "children": [
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "text": "What are the pOH and the pH of a 0.025-M solution of potassium hydroxide, KOH?"
                  }
                ],
                "id": "97qw2jys6drrlw5",
                "type": "p"
              },
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "text": "Potassium hydroxide is a highly soluble ionic compound that completely dissociates in dilute solution. Each KOH formula unit yields one K"
                  },
                  {
                    "sup": true,
                    "text": "+"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ion and one OH"
                  },
                  {
                    "sup": true,
                    "text": "−"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ion, so the [OH"
                  },
                  {
                    "sup": true,
                    "text": "−"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "] = 0.025 M. First calculate the pOH:"
                  }
                ],
                "id": "xtyjt7npyaya15t",
                "type": "p"
              },
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "id": "96a4vgi91cymefm",
                    "text": " ",
                    "type": "text"
                  }
                ],
                "id": "frambuwaxhax89q",
                "legacyBlockRendered": "true",
                "src": "\\mathrm{pOH}\\;=\\;-\\log\\lbrack\\mathrm{OH}^-\\rbrack\\;=\\;-\\log(0.025)\\;=\\;1.60",
                "subtype": "latex",
                "type": "formula"
              },
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "text": "The pH can be found from the pOH:"
                  }
                ],
                "id": "036476kv548eqdl",
                "type": "p"
              },
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "id": "gvxw4syo6mvzyeq",
                    "text": " ",
                    "type": "text"
                  }
                ],
                "id": "l91c7vx32fdh4jn",
                "legacyBlockRendered": "true",
                "src": "\\mathrm{pH}\\;+\\;\\mathrm{pOH}\\;=\\;14.00",
                "subtype": "latex",
                "type": "formula"
              },
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "id": "ha4olxnsqev8fri",
                    "text": " ",
                    "type": "text"
                  }
                ],
                "id": "q8mkbi1i8nc97zm",
                "legacyBlockRendered": "true",
                "src": "\\mathrm{pH}\\;=\\;14.00\\;-\\;\\mathrm{pOH}\\;=\\;14.00\\;-\\;1.60\\;=\\;12.40",
                "subtype": "latex",
                "type": "formula"
              },
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "text": ""
                  }
                ],
                "id": "2044878540",
                "type": "p"
              }
            ],
            "id": "4257393659",
            "selection": {
              "anchor": {
                "offset": 0,
