          }
        ],
        "id": "2286706649",
        "layout": "vertical",
        "purpose": "example",
        "type": "group"
      },
      {
        "children": [
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "text": "What are the pOH and the pH of a 0.030-M solution of barium hydroxide, Ba(OH)"
                  },
                  {
                    "sub": true,
                    "text": "2"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "?"
                  }
                ],
                "id": "b7wohwrlwwzf60y",
                "type": "p"
              },
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "text": "Barium hydroxide is also a soluble ionic compound that completely dissociates in dilute solution. Each Ba(OH)"
                  },
                  {
                    "sub": true,
                    "text": "2"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " formula unit yields one Ba"
                  },
                  {
                    "sup": true,
                    "text": "2+"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ion and two OH"
                  },
                  {
                    "sup": true,
                    "text": "−"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ions, so the [OH"
                  },
                  {
                    "sup": true,
                    "text": "−"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "] = 2 × (0.030 M) = 0.060 M. Calculate the pOH:"
                  }
                ],
                "id": "l6kf969m1h57ez3",
                "type": "p"
              },
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "id": "nwb98fznkrwy04d",
                    "text": " ",
                    "type": "text"
                  }
                ],
                "id": "hipjhub8vjrc1wy",
                "legacyBlockRendered": "true",
                "src": "\\mathrm{pOH}\\;=\\;-\\log\\lbrack\\mathrm{OH}^-\\rbrack\\;=\\;-\\log(0.060)\\;=\\;1.22",
                "subtype": "latex",
                "type": "formula"
              },
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "text": "Then calculate the pH from the pOH:"
                  }
                ],
                "id": "ptcf3zi2of92d7f",
                "type": "p"
              },
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "id": "o4i5ok4f8rreuoa",
                    "text": " ",
                    "type": "text"
                  }
                ],
                "id": "4iuyhhbzu66esbd",
                "legacyBlockRendered": "true",
                "src": "\\mathrm{pH}\\;+\\;\\mathrm{pOH}\\;=\\;14.00",
                "subtype": "latex",
                "type": "formula"
              },
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "id": "mtqbjqygv5qs3i2",
                    "text": " ",
                    "type": "text"
                  }
                ],
                "id": "l8fvkzv03gmkgoc",
                "legacyBlockRendered": "true",
                "src": "\\mathrm{pH}\\;=\\;14.00\\;-\\;\\mathrm{pOH}\\;=\\;14.00\\;-\\;1.22\\;=\\;12.78",
                "subtype": "latex",
                "type": "formula"
              },
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "text": ""
                  }
                ],
                "id": "1736689612",
                "type": "p"
              }
            ],
